{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
  "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James R. Milkey, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If I may, I'd like to frame the merits very quickly and then turn immediately to standing. Although the case before you arises in an important policy area, it turns on ordinary principles of statutory interpretation and administrative law. EPA made a decision based on two grounds, both of which constitute plain errors of law reviewable under any standard."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought that the standing requires imminent harm. If you haven't been harmed already, you have to show the harm is imminent. Is this harm imminent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James R. Milkey, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For example, Congress itself expressly referred to carbon dioxide as an air pollutant in section 103(g). And since by definition all air pollutants are air pollution agents, we know that Congress understood carbon dioxide to be an agent of air pollution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "James R. Milkey, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "EPA has a lot of room to move based both on the endangerment standard itself and on background principles of administrative law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Milkey",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MILKEY: Your Honor, while background administrative law principles provide EPA at least some room to move, we think it's important that EPA say that. If they -- it's a very different opinion if they say, we are not going to regular here because we just don't want to spend the resources on this problem and we want to look elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Milkey",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They're both effects. I would point you to the example of acid rain, where the pollutant there, sulfur dioxide, the problem is it causes its harm after it leaves the air, after it gets washed out. Air pollutants do not need to cause harm in the ambient air."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Gregory G. Garre",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "After carefully considering the issue the nation's expert agency in environmental matters concluded that Congress has not authorized it to embark on the regulation of greenhouse gas emissions to address global climate change. And that even if it has, now is not the time to exercise such authority, in light of the substantial scientific uncertainty surrounding global climate change and the ongoing studies designed to address those uncertainties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF GREGORY G. GARRE, ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ballunas",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0001-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ballunas amicus brief -- I think it is fair for the Court to look at, to look at the document that the agency had before it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: But do you have any --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So they couldn't have gone in and asked for ozone regulations, because that requires other countries? Or what about dumping heavy metals in the sea, and as the sea gets polluted because of what other countries do, but EPA tried to regulate that. Acid rain they tried to regulate. You're saying there is no standing to ask for any of that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "EPA",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Your Honor, what I would point you to is your decision in Lujan versus Defenders of Wildlife, Justice Kennedy's opinion in ASARCO versus Kadish, where the Court made clear that you cannot establish standing based on predictions of the actions of independent actors not before it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: As I understand the government's position, you're not merely questioning standing but you also take the position you do not have the authority to do what the plaintiff asks you to do; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Can I ask about that? I found persuasive Solicitor General Garre's point that in the acid rain context, it isn't air pollution that harms health, but rather it is the effect of the pollutant after it leaves the air and produces the acid rain. Is there anything wrong with that response? It seems to me --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If the EPA concludes that regulating an air pollutant would endanger public health and welfare, can it decline to regulate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c08ac479a8f8-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Isn't the definition of public welfare extremely broad?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1120",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "c08ac479a8f8432f9a66b74898c2de08a7c081cf82a87968b748cadffe6c9fcf",
